<title>PANAMA: Panama to reduce tariffs on technology products.</title>
<headline>Panama to reduce tariffs on technology products.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panama became the first Latin American country to sign a World Trade Organization (WTO) agreement which will reduce tariffs on technology products by the year 2000, Treasury Minister Miguel Heras said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Under the information technology agreement, tariffs on computers, computer parts, telecommunications equipment and semiconductors will be reduced to zero by the year 2000, he said.</p>
<p>Panama is one of 28 countries to sign on to the agreement and &quot;the first Latin American nation to take this initiative as world markets open up,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
<p>The measure is due to go into effect in June.</p>
<p>((-- Laurens Grant, Panama City newsroom, 507 2237739))</p>
